From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: XPRESS_HUFF never sends the match of distance 1 and length 3

That match is the symbol 256, which ends a stream: the decoder takes it
as the end once the input is used up, so an input ending in it lost its
tail ("qzzzz" came back as "qz", 65539 zeros as 65536: the second 64 KiB
block was three zeros). It is sent as literals.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XZFS4SPPzeH5d2c1MuzqCS
---

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/rtl.c b/dlls/ntdll/rtl.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/rtl.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/rtl.c
@@ -1621,6 +1621,13 @@
         {
             ULONG dist = 0, len = xpress_find_match( &m, pos, end, &dist );
 
+            /* a match of distance 1 and length 3 would be the symbol 256, the end of the stream:
+             * the decoder reads it as the end once the input is used up (the tail of "qzzzz" and
+             * of 65539 zeros was lost); it is sent as literals */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_XPRESS_OFF1
+            if (len == 3 && dist == 1) len = 0;
+#endif
+
             if (!len)
             {
                 items[count].length = 0;
